##### lab-j  192.168.1.20  scope lab  juniper (TACACS+) #####
# Based on the pull of <time> by alice over netconf (less than a minute ago; the login could
# see secrets) and the standard of <time> (tacctl 0.2.0-test).
#
# What is irregular on lab-j (2 items; the paste fixes 2, leaves 0):
#  1. mgmt-acl ACCESS     missing: the management filter MGMT-ACL: 8 statements (e.g. set firewall
#                         family inet filter MGMT-ACL term permit-tcp-22 from source-address
#                         198.51.100.0/24). Fixed by region lines 3-10.
#  2. mgmt-acl ACCESS     extra: the management filter MGMT-ACL: 10 statements (e.g. set firewall
#                         family inet filter MGMT-ACL term permit-mgmt from source-address
#                         198.51.100.0/24). Fixed by region lines 11-16.
# Not planned: netconf, breakglass (walkthrough Steps 6 and 7).
# Not selected (--section): roles, aaa, snmp.
# WARNING: the management filter of 'lab' is strict: it has no default-accept term. The device applies
# it to lo0 already, so from the commit the device accepts traffic to its routing engine only from the
# sources of the permit list (10.0.0.42/32, 10.0.0.0/8, 198.51.100.0/24) and the SNMP clients, and
# these stop: routing protocols carried over IP from neighbours that are not in the list (BGP, OSPF,
# LDP, VRRP, BFD); TACACS+ and RADIUS replies from servers that are not in the list (those of the
# server the walkthrough names are accepted); NTP, syslog and DHCP from hosts that are not in the
# list; SNMP from sources outside the list (the SNMP clients still poll); every other protocol from
# sources outside it. A family inet filter on lo0 does not affect IS-IS (it is not carried over IP):
# this filter neither stops nor permits it. Keep a console session open while you paste, and add every
# neighbour and server the device needs to the permit list the scope renders from first (the first
# entry of the scope's own list replaces the global list for the scope).
# The switch undoes this by itself in 5 minutes unless you type the one word after the check (see
# below).
# Paste over ssh, not the console; on a console paste at most twenty lines at a time and watch the
# echo for 'error:'. Pasting the region twice is harmless.
#
# Type this first, on lab-j, and check the name:   show version | match Hostname
# The prompt must end in > (operational mode) before you paste: a prompt ending in # means a
# configuration session is open: stop.
# The region opens configure exclusive: the session holds the configuration lock until you type exit
# (after commit, to confirm). If it printed "error: configuration database modified", another session
# has uncommitted changes: have that person commit or discard them, then paste again. If it printed
# "error: configuration database locked by", another session holds the exclusive lock: wait for it to
# exit, then paste again. Either way nothing happened (every later line is an unknown command).
#
##### PASTE FROM HERE: lab-j #####
configure exclusive
# mgmt-acl: the management filter tacctl renders (its terms, their leaves and their order)
set firewall family inet filter MGMT-ACL term permit-tcp-22 from source-address 198.51.100.0/24
set firewall family inet filter MGMT-ACL term permit-tcp-22 from protocol tcp
set firewall family inet filter MGMT-ACL term permit-tcp-22 from destination-port ssh
set firewall family inet filter MGMT-ACL term permit-tcp-22 then accept
set firewall family inet filter MGMT-ACL term permit-udp-161 from source-address 198.51.100.0/24
set firewall family inet filter MGMT-ACL term permit-udp-161 from protocol udp
set firewall family inet filter MGMT-ACL term permit-udp-161 from destination-port snmp
set firewall family inet filter MGMT-ACL term permit-udp-161 then accept
delete firewall family inet filter MGMT-ACL term permit-mgmt from source-address 198.51.100.0/24
delete firewall family inet filter MGMT-ACL term permit-mgmt from protocol tcp
delete firewall family inet filter MGMT-ACL term permit-mgmt from destination-port ssh
delete firewall family inet filter MGMT-ACL term permit-mgmt from destination-port 830
delete firewall family inet filter MGMT-ACL term deny-mgmt
delete firewall family inet filter MGMT-ACL term default-accept
show | compare | no-more
commit check
commit confirmed 5 comment "tacctl plan lab-j <time> by alice"
##### PASTE TO HERE: lab-j #####
#
# If the first line printed "error: configuration database modified" or "error: configuration
# database locked by": nothing happened (see the note above the region); paste again once it is
# cleared. If any line printed "error:": do not type commit; the switch undoes this by itself in 5
# minutes.
#
# Check now. In 5 minutes the switch undoes this by itself unless you type one word.
#   From the tacctl server:   tacctl device config pull lab-j --diff     (mgmt-acl: ok)
#   In a second terminal:     ssh lab-j, then: show cli authorization | no-more
#                             show configuration firewall family inet filter MGMT-ACL | no-more
# When both checks are fine, type this one word yourself:  commit     (before the 5 minutes end)
# Then type exit: the session holds the configuration lock until you do.
#
# If your session drops before that, the switch still rolls back when the time runs out (a dropped
# CLI session does not roll back at once): log in again and paste again.
# To undo it after the commit: tacctl device config plan lab-j --backout (its own region to paste;
# tacctl keeps this plan's back-out: after the check pull has replaced the picture, the command
# still prints this plan's, and says which pull it undoes, until the next plan with changes).
# Without tacctl: show system commit, then rollback <n> of the entry just before the one commented
# "tacctl plan lab-j" (the newest entry is that commit itself), then commit.
# Do not: type commit before the check; paste anything outside the banners; paste this into
# another device; keep this output in a file after the paste when it holds a secret.
# Locked out (the paste cut your session and no login works)? A superuser runs: tacctl breakglass hold lab-j --reason "..."
# then log in as the device's local user (ssh or console),
# fix or back out, and the superuser runs: tacctl breakglass release lab-j
